  "base": "the frozen model 1.1.0 (candidate s5): kinetics: ln f(t) = L(t) (1 - rho W(t)); L(t) = ell + e r(t) + s q(t), r = exp(-(t - t1)/tau), q = exp(-(t - t1)/14 days), t1 = 1 day, t in months, f = central thickness / pretreatment thickness, ell = context level + b ln(CST0 / 300 um); W(t) = 1/(1 + exp(-(t - D)/w)) for series with a declared single-dose duration D, else W = 0; dose_rule: one dexamethasone implant (regimen single; treatment steroid_implant unless the agent names fluocinolone, or combination when the agent names a dexamethasone implant): D = 3.5 months, w = 0.5 months, rho = 0.8; every other group has no duration (retina_thickness_population_1_1.effect_duration_months); deviations: forecast-only Ornstein-Uhlenbeck deviations (phi 0.8, 12 months) as in model 1.0.0; the population is fitted under working independence; noise: Gaussian in ln f; group-mean SD scaled by (n/40)^-g with g estimated in each fit, clipped to [0, 0.5]; likelihood centre = median of study residual SDs, a new study's SD marginalized over log-normal(log-SD 0.5) around the scaled centre, floor 0.01; forecast intervals add independent noise of variance sigma^2 ((c_pooled/c_median)^2 - 1), c_pooled = sqrt(sum(dof sd^2)/sum(dof)) over the same study estimates of the same fit; hierarchy: one hierarchy per species: species mean, shared level slope by GLS inside REML, context, study and series deviations; diagonal covariances by penalized REML (Gamma(2) SD modes 0.1, 0.1, 0.1, 0.5)",
  "stacking": "eye_stacking 1.0.0: forecasts from follow-up = w_model population_assimilation + w_persistence last observation + w_increment pooled-curve increment (pooled_curve_ratio); initial states = w_model population_initial_state + w_curve pooled training curve; a missing member drops out with the other weights renormalized; intervals = the model variant's quantiles moved to the stacked point (width unchanged)",
